---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro"

const title = "Raghav Sharma — Product Engineer"
const description = "Portfolio of Raghav Sharma, a product engineer building developer tools, AI products, and blockchain infrastructure with Rust and TypeScript."
const external = { target: "_blank", rel: "noopener noreferrer" }
const schema = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@graph": [
    { "@type": "WebSite", "@id": "https://raghav.codes/#website", url: "https://raghav.codes/", name: "Raghav Sharma — Raghav Codes", description, inLanguage: "en", publisher: { "@id": "https://raghav.codes/#raghav-sharma" } },
    { "@type": "Person", "@id": "https://raghav.codes/#raghav-sharma", name: "Raghav Sharma", url: "https://raghav.codes/", image: "https://raghav.codes/og.png", description: "Product engineer building developer tools, AI products, and blockchain infrastructure with Rust and TypeScript.", jobTitle: "Product Engineer", knowsAbout: ["Rust", "TypeScript", "backend systems", "AI agents", "blockchain infrastructure", "Solana"], sameAs: ["https://github.com/some1uknow", "https://www.linkedin.com/in/raghavsharmaweb3", "https://x.com/raghavdotsol"] },
  ],
}
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description}>
  <main id="main-content" class="page-shell">
    <header class="profile-header">
      <div class="identity">
        <img src="/favicon.svg" width="56" height="56" alt="" class="avatar" />
        <div><h1>Raghav Sharma</h1><p>Product engineer</p></div>
      </div>
      <nav class="contact-links" aria-label="Contact and social links">
        <a href="https://github.com/some1uknow" {...external}>
          <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 2a10 10 0 0 0-3.16 19.49c.5.09.68-.22.68-.48v-1.88c-2.78.6-3.37-1.18-3.37-1.18-.45-1.16-1.11-1.47-1.11-1.47-.91-.62.07-.61.07-.61 1 .07 1.53 1.03 1.53 1.03.9 1.53 2.35 1.09 2.92.83.09-.65.35-1.09.64-1.34-2.22-.25-4.55-1.11-4.55-4.94 0-1.09.39-1.98 1.03-2.68-.1-.25-.45-1.27.1-2.64 0 0 .84-.27 2.75 1.02A9.6 9.6 0 0 1 12 6.82a9.6 9.6 0 0 1 2.5.34c1.91-1.3 2.75-1.02 2.75-1.02.55 1.37.2 2.39.1 2.64.64.7 1.03 1.59 1.03 2.68 0 3.84-2.34 4.68-4.57 4.93.36.31.68.92.68 1.86v2.76c0 .27.18.58.69.48A10 10 0 0 0 12 2Z" /></svg>
          <span>github</span>
        </a>
        <a href="https://x.com/raghavdotsol" {...external}>
          <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M18.9 2H22l-6.77 7.74L23.2 22h-6.24l-4.89-6.39L6.48 22H3.36l7.23-8.27L2.95 2h6.4l4.42 5.84L18.9 2Zm-1.1 17.84h1.73L8.41 4.05H6.56L17.8 19.84Z" /></svg>
          <span>x</span>
        </a>
        <a href="https://linkedin.com/in/raghavsharmaweb3" {...external}>
          <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M6.5 8.4H3.2V21h3.3V8.4ZM4.85 3A1.92 1.92 0 1 0 4.85 6.84 1.92 1.92 0 0 0 4.85 3ZM21 13.8c0-3.8-2.03-5.57-4.74-5.57-2.18 0-3.16 1.2-3.7 2.04V8.4H9.25V21h3.31v-6.24c0-1.65.31-3.25 2.36-3.25 2.02 0 2.04 1.89 2.04 3.36V21H21v-7.2Z" /></svg>
          <span>linkedin</span>
        </a>
        <a href="mailto:raghu250407@gmail.com">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M3 5h18v14H3V5Zm2 2v.5l7 4.67 7-4.67V7H5Zm14 10V9.9l-7 4.66L5 9.9V17h14Z" /></svg>
          <span>email</span>
        </a>
        <a href="/blog">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 3h11l3 3v15H5V3Zm2 2v14h10V7h-2V5H7Zm2 5h6v2H9v-2Zm0 4h6v2H9v-2Z" /></svg>
          <span>writings</span>
        </a>
      </nav>
    </header>

    <section class="narrative" aria-labelledby="about-label">
      <h2 id="about-label">About</h2>
      <p>I learnt by building things on the internet. What started as curiosity slowly turned into an obsession with understanding how software works beneath the surface — the systems, infrastructure, and weird edge cases that make products actually work.</p>
      <p>I mostly write <span class="brand brand--rust"><img src="https://cdn.simpleicons.org/rust/CE422B" width="13" height="13" alt="" />Rust</span> and <span class="brand brand--typescript"><img src="https://cdn.simpleicons.org/typescript/3178C6" width="13" height="13" alt="" />TypeScript</span>. Over time, that pulled me deeper into backend systems, developer tools, and blockchain infrastructure, where I could learn by building things that had to work beyond a demo.</p>
      <p>I founded <a class="brand brand--learnsol has-preview" href="https://learnsol.site" {...external}><img src="https://www.learnsol.site/icon.png" width="13" height="13" alt="" />LearnSol<span class="brand-preview"><img src="/previews/learnsol.webp" width="640" height="416" alt="" /></span></a>, a hands-on Solana and Rust learning platform used by 2,200+ developers. I built its curriculum, retrieval system, sandbox, and production stack, and received a $5,000 <a class="brand brand--solana" href="https://solana.org/" {...external}><img src="https://cdn.simpleicons.org/solana/14F195" width="13" height="13" alt="" />Solana Foundation</a> grant for the work.</p>
      <p>Since then, I’ve kept shipping and experimenting. I built <a class="brand brand--cipherpay has-preview" href="https://www.cipherpay.fun" {...external}><img src="/icons/cipherpay.png" width="13" height="13" alt="" />CipherPay<span class="brand-preview"><img src="/previews/cipherpay.webp" width="640" height="416" alt="" /></span></a> for private payroll and batch payouts on Solana, <a class="brand brand--ezdeploy has-preview" href="https://ezdeploy.raghav.codes" {...external}><img src="https://ezdeploy.raghav.codes/icon.svg" width="13" height="13" alt="" />EzDeploy<span class="brand-preview"><img src="/previews/ezdeploy.webp" width="640" height="416" alt="" /></span></a> for deploying static GitHub projects in a click, and a bunch of smaller systems across payments, protocols, indexing, and infrastructure.</p>
      <p>Along the way, I worked as a software engineering intern at <a class="brand brand--fossee" href="https://fossee.in" {...external}><img class="brand-logo--wide" src="/icons/fossee.png" width="13" height="13" alt="" />FOSSEE, IIT Bombay</a> and <a class="brand brand--debales" href="https://debales.ai" {...external}><img src="/icons/debales.png" width="13" height="13" alt="" />Debales AI</a>, won <a class="brand brand--sih" href="https://www.sih.gov.in/sih2024/sih2024-grand-finale-result" {...external}><img class="brand-logo--wide" src="/icons/smart-india-hackathon.png" width="13" height="13" alt="" />Smart India Hackathon</a>, had my work featured by <a class="brand brand--colosseum" href="https://blog.colosseum.com/audit-subsidy-program-learnsol-umbra/" {...external}><img src="/icons/colosseum.png" width="13" height="13" alt="" />Colosseum</a>, and became a member of <a class="brand brand--superteam" href="https://in.superteam.fun/" {...external}><img src="/icons/superteam.png" width="13" height="13" alt="" />Superteam India</a>.</p>
      <p>Lately, I’ve been going deep on AI agents — building my own products around them and experimenting with how agents use tools, make decisions, move money, and interact with software without a human sitting in the middle.</p>
      <p>It feels like the next rabbit hole I want to spend a long time exploring.</p>
      <p>I’m now looking for my first full-time role at an awesome startup, working with people who care deeply about what they build. I want to ship ambitious products, learn ridiculously fast, and get very good at building things that are hard to make simple.</p>
    </section>
    <footer><p>© 2026 Raghav Sharma</p></footer>
  </main>
  <script is:inline type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(schema)} />
</BaseLayout>
